<div class=3D"comment reply"><div class=3D"comment__meta"><span class=3D"co=
mment__author">A Fandom user</span> <span class=3D"comment__date">2013-11-1=
2 01:51 UTC</span></div><div class=3D"comment__body"><p>There is no scripte=
d "success" in the sense of "no matter what it's 9+". &nbsp;You can trigger=
 the "success" you're talking about as early as Y2 if you build the custom =
engine early. &nbsp;In reality, there are two scripted "no hits" followed b=
y a scripted "hit".
</p><p>You initially compete against a score of around 30*. &nbsp;Typically=
, matching the target score results in a review score of 9**. &nbsp;In the =
beginning, however, the first two review scores that are at least 9 instead=
 score around 8. &nbsp;During the sales of these games, an announcement is =
made calling them "surprise hits".
</p><p>The third review score that is at least 9 will instead result in a p=
erfect 10/10/10/9. &nbsp;This will garner massive sales and "launch you out=
 of the garage". &nbsp;From then on, you compete against your previous scor=
es.
</p>
<ul><li>30 combined design/tech points with no bugs or penalties and all bo=
nuses except for trend.</li></ul>
<ul><li><ul><li>Actual displayed review scores will be 9 +/- 1.</li></ul></=
li></ul></div></div>
</div>
</div>
