ty, even if it would be a 0.00001% decrease (which would eventually matter =
not, but still it is a bug ratio of less than 1)
</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"comment"><div class=3D"comment__meta"><span class=3D"comment_=
_author">A Fandom user</span> <span class=3D"comment__date">2013-05-07 22:4=
1 UTC</span></div><div class=3D"comment__body"><p>This is more confusing th=
an the main wiki game development page where this was advertised.
</p><p>I still am yet to know exactly what ratios of tech/design to use. so=
metimes it is 1:1 ratio and I get 9.5+. Sometimes it is a 1:1 ratio, same t=
opic, same genre, same sliders, same everything, identical in every way, an=
d then gets 3.
</p><p>It's not really a fun game when you basically have to have a wiki pa=
ge open and parrot fashion particular numbers, which if you deviate by a sm=
all amount, gives you terrible reviews and lost money. It's even less fun w=
hen it seems completely random, and works brilliantly one time and doesn't =
work at all the next despite being identical just to cream in some money in=
 the early days.
</p><p>This game is pretty random, and when you think you've figured it out=
 throws back a garbled mess. Even if I did have the time to figure it out, =
it just isn't fun. I want to play a game to have fun, not to have a mental =
mathematics lesson.
</p></div>
<div class=3D"replies">
<div class=3D"comment reply"><div class=3D"comment__meta"><span class=3D"co=
mment__author">Istrebitel</span> <span class=3D"comment__date">2013-05-08 0=
8:22 UTC</span> <span class=3D"comment__edited">(edited)</span></div><div c=
lass=3D"comment__body"><p>This game is very precise and cosistent. There is=
 little to no randomness involved at all (after you start getting over 100 =
points in Design + Tech, only randomness you really get is the trend, every=
thing else is absolutely predictable).
</p><p>Follow the guide from start to end and you will learn about why you =
get 9.5+ and then consequently get 3's, this gudie IS done mostly in order =
to explain THIS VERY QUIRK of the game.
</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
